From 82b63bc32d0f8e107d81d5a8d0e981d4a5b312ff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: James Clark <james.clark@arm.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Nov 2022 17:50:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1166/1646] [Backport] perf cs-etm: Create ETE decoder

mainline inclusion
from mainline-v5.15-rc1
commit 779f414a4849fb3e650cad8525c84e76fdd3c0ea
category: feature
bugzilla: https://gitee.com/openeuler/kernel/issues/I636PS

Reference: https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/commit/?id=779f414a4849fb3e650cad8525c84e76fdd3c0ea

--------------------------------

If the magic number indicates ETE instantiate a OCSD_BUILTIN_DCD_ETE
decoder instead of OCSD_BUILTIN_DCD_ETMV4I. ETE is the new trace feature
for Armv9.

Testing performed
=================

* Old files with v0 and v1 headers for ETMv4 still open correctly
* New files with new magic number open on new versions of perf
* New files with new magic number fail to open on old versions of perf
* Decoding with the ETE decoder results in the same output as the ETMv4
  decoder as long as there are no new ETE packet types

